public inherited sharing class AccountRatingService {
    private static final String HOT_RATING = 'Hot';
    private static final String WARM_RATING = 'Warm';
    private static final String COLD_RATING = 'Cold';
    private static final Decimal HOT_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD = 100000;

    @future
    public static void recalculate(List<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Set<Id> uniqueAccountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Id accountId : accountIds) {
            if (accountId != null) {
                uniqueAccountIds.add(accountId);
            }
        }

        if (uniqueAccountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, Decimal> maxAmountByAccount = new Map<Id, Decimal>();

        for (AggregateResult result : [
            SELECT AccountId, MAX(Amount) maxAmount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :uniqueAccountIds
              AND IsClosed = false
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            Id accountId = (Id) result.get('AccountId');
            Decimal maxAmount = (Decimal) result.get('maxAmount');
            maxAmountByAccount.put(accountId, maxAmount);
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();

        for (Id accountId : uniqueAccountIds) {
            String rating = COLD_RATING;

            if (maxAmountByAccount.containsKey(accountId)) {
                Decimal maxAmount = maxAmountByAccount.get(accountId);
                rating = (maxAmount != null && maxAmount >= HOT_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD)
                    ? HOT_RATING
                    : WARM_RATING;
            }

            accountsToUpdate.add(new Account(Id = accountId, Rating = rating));
        }

        Database.update(accountsToUpdate, false);
    }
}
```

Note: I did not make one future call per opportunity. With 200 opportunities in a single transaction, that would exceed the Apex governor limit of 50 future method calls per transaction. Instead, the trigger collects affected account IDs and makes one `@future` call with `List<Id>`, keeping it bulk-safe while still asynchronous.

